, "v4EJbM": {"type":"text","parent":"g22AP4","order":"a1","name":"Value","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"Tied to the links' pulse (Edges, motion spec): every link runs on one 2.4 s clock and its glow lands at the input port 1.6 s in. Each time, a puff of new cloud swells out in a circle from each connected port on the card's left edge: about 15 cells at most, easing out over 1 s, with a cloud's uneven edge and a denser middle. It's added to the cloud's own thickness, so it has the same solid core, particle edges, light and shade as any puff, and runs together with the cloud and with neighbouring ports' puffs. It carries a touch of the link's glow as it appears and settles into the sky within the cycle. The rest of the card doesn't move for it. Unconnected ports take nothing; waiting cards take no puffs.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":"Inter","size":12,"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.5},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

